U3B'S EFFICIENCY OVER THE MODEL'S OWN HOURS (u3b_hourly.py, stream s119, S-119, second round). AI arithmetic on the
makers' figures (SLUSE66A Equations 6 to 22 via records/s117/efficiency.py); nothing built or measured; core loss and
light-load PFM excluded. Buck-boost bound at every hour; VIN the model's node voltage, VOUT its lid voltage. The
weighting takes every hour; at the lightest (under 5 W, the taper's tail) fixed losses dominate and the equations read
low, down to 0 where they exceed the input, which PFM would soften; those hours carry little energy (printed).

