THE FIGURE CARRIED (the 400 kHz row): the lowest weighted TI figure over the eight cases, rounded down, 0.972 (range
0.9724 to 0.9736); bracket 0.963 (the lowest at the makers' maxima) to 0.978 (the highest at the most favourable reading).
Way (a) at 800 kHz on the same hours, for comparison: 0.9572 to 0.9596; worst hour of 5 W or more 0.906.
The peak-hour figures of efficiency.out section 7 (0.974 at 400 kHz, 0.961 at 800 kHz) sit above these: the peak is
U3B's most favourable load, and its light hours cost more in proportion.
END.
